    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1532">

                <pb facs="0985" n="869" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg869"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.51/57.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The French Chargé &amp;
                            Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">French Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Manchester</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 16, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I beg to thank your excellency for what the Department of State has already done
                    in regard to French citizens imprisoned at Zacatecas. Pending the moment when
                    the President and yourself will be able to receive me I should be greatly
                    obliged to your excellency if he would prescribe an immediate inquest tending to
                    ascertain the correctness of the information that reached our Legation in Mexico
                    City concerning the murder of two French Christian Brothers, Messrs. Astru and
                    Gilles, shot at Zacatecas on Villa’s order and if he would keep me informed of
                    the result of that inquest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clausse</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
